doc:agreementConcerningEsoc a schema:Legislation ;
    rdfs:label "Agreement concerning ESOC"@en ;
    schema:description "Agreement concluded between the Government of the Federal Republic of Germany and ESRO to establish a European Space Operations Centre, including the European Space Data Centre; Articles 1 to 4 concern the site and related matters."@en ;
    schema:hasPart doc:article_6_agreement_concerning_esoc .

doc:applicantsLawyers a schema:Role ;
    rdfs:label "applicants' lawyers (as named in the procedure)"@en .

doc:article6_issue_access_to_court_1 a echr:Article6Issue ;
    rdfs:label "Alleged denial of access to a tribunal under Article 6 § 1 (ESA immunity)"@en ;
    echr:affectsParty doc:applicants_1 ;
    echr:hasIssueDescription "The applicants contended that they had not had a fair hearing by a tribunal on the question whether a contractual relationship existed between them and ESA and alleged a violation of Article 6 § 1 of the Convention."@en ;
    echr:issueArisesIn doc:domesticProceedingLabourCourtDarmstadt .

doc:articleIiEsaConvention a schema:Legislation ;
    rdfs:label "Article II of the ESA Convention"@en ;
    schema:description "States the purpose of ESA to provide for and promote, for exclusively peaceful purposes, cooperation among European States in space research and technology and their space applications, with a view to scientific purposes and operational space applications systems."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf doc:esaConvention .

doc:articleViEsaConvention a schema:Legislation ;
    rdfs:label "Article VI of the ESA Convention"@en ;
    schema:description "Provides that for the execution of entrusted programmes the Agency shall maintain internal capability required for preparation and supervision of its tasks and shall establish and operate such establishments and facilities as required for its activities (Article VI § 1 (a)); agreements concerning the headquarters and establishments shall be concluded between the Agency and the member States concerned (Article VI § 3)."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf doc:esaConvention .

doc:articleXvEsaConvention a schema:Legislation ;
    rdfs:label "Article XV of the ESA Convention"@en ;
    schema:description "Regulates the legal status, privileges and immunities of the Agency, including that the Agency shall have legal personality and that the Agency, its staff members and experts, and representatives of member States shall enjoy capacities, privileges and immunities provided for in Annex I."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf doc:esaConvention .

doc:articleXviiEsaConvention a schema:Legislation ;
    rdfs:label "Article XVII of the ESA Convention"@en ;
    schema:description "Concerns the arbitration procedure in case of disputes between member States or between any of them and ESA concerning interpretation or application of the Convention or its annexes, and disputes arising out of damage caused by ESA not settled by the Council."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf doc:esaConvention .

doc:article_6_agreement_concerning_esoc a schema:Legislation ;
    rdfs:label "Article 6 of the Agreement concerning ESOC"@en ;
    schema:description "Provides that disputes between the Organisation and such staff members of the Organisation in the Federal Republic of Germany who are not within the competence of the Organisation's Appeals Board shall be subject to German jurisdiction."@en,
        "States that, subject to the Protocol on Privileges and Immunities and any complementary Agreement under Article 30 of that Protocol, the activities of the Organisation in the Federal Republic of Germany shall be governed by German law; if the terms of employment of a staff member are not governed by the Organisation's staff regulations, they shall be subject to German laws and regulations."@en ;
    schema:isPartOf doc:agreementConcerningEsoc ;
    schema:mentions doc:esro,
        doc:governmentOfFederalRepublicOfGermany .

